atlas context

architecture attention-cooling
  canonical_name AttentionCoolingGraph
  family context
  domain Context / Attention
  layer context
  semantic_question What deserves attention now, and what has cooled until a named signal reheats it?
  purpose Scheduling as reheat conditions, not a cron table. Run 6's scheduling unit was "all five planes finished supercycle N", so a static blocker (Proton) kept consuming frontier attention forever. This cools a subject against a named reheat condition; only a matching signal reheats it. The same discipline the ProofFrontier applies to knowledge, applied to attention.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Subject
  node_types Temperature
  edge_types cools
  edge_types reheats
  state_types hot
  state_types warm
  state_types cold
  internal_calculus temperature with named reheat conditions
  invariant a cooled subject must name what reheats it, or it consumes attention forever
  invariant only a signal matching a named reheat condition may reheat a cooled subject
  forbidden_inference a symptom -> attention (only a named reheat signal warms a cooled subject)
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/scheduling.py.archive
  source_path engine/core/src/control_attention.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAttention/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreAttention/tests/smoke.sh
  interacts proof-frontier
  interacts work-graph
  source_lineage run6 control-plane retrospective -- the Proton attention-drain fix; native persistence absorption retains the shared watches schema
  known_gap Python scheduling callers remain on the compatibility carrier until their call boundaries move to BonfyreAttention

architecture atlas-context-provider
  owns AtlasAnswer
  publishes AtlasAnswer
  derived AtlasAnswer
  canonical_name AtlasContextProvider
  family context
  domain Context / Model Context
  layer context
  semantic_question What does one atlas question cost to answer, and can it cost only that?
  purpose A lossless registry is not a context surface. atlas.index.json is 257,986 bytes; delivering it to answer "what does ProviderGraph forbid?" spends ~64k tokens to carry ~200 tokens of answer. This is the bounded read path: summary/get/search/cannot_infer/expand/loss computed from the exported index, every op under a byte budget, search reading field VALUES rather than the JSON serialization (which made every schema key searchable content -- search("witness") returned all 185 architectures). Query semantics live here once, so the CLI, MCP transport, CI and native callers cannot drift.
  maturity measured
  node_types Query
  node_types BoundedAnswer
  edge_types answers
  edge_types truncates
  internal_calculus value-walk (keys are schema, never content)
  internal_calculus per-response byte budget with explicit truncation
  invariant every op declares a byte budget and reports truncation rather than silently exceeding it
  invariant search matches field values and the architecture id, never field names
  invariant explain fields (matched_fields, snippet) are request-local and never enter the exported index
  invariant the Bun MCP project owner invokes the same root-relative Bun query command as the Atlas CLI and deploy witness; transport does not reimplement search, provenance or byte budgeting
  forbidden_inference a bounded answer -> the registry is lossy (the registry stays lossless; only the read path is bounded)
  forbidden_inference cheapest read path -> authoritative answer (the index is derived; the YaFF registry is canonical)
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/main.c
  source_path architecture/atlas.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_reads.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_node.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_node_cutover.json records the installed Bun project owner serving the root-local Atlas query over HTTP
  witness bun test architecture/tests/atlas_query.test.mjs exercises bounded value-only search, explicit misses, request-local explanation and provenance
  interacts realization-measurement
  source_lineage run8 provider-context-pressure -- measured 559.6x context reduction per lookup
  known_gap only the atlas is served this way; the same bounded-read discipline is unapplied to the fabric and evidence surfaces
  known_gap the installed Bun project owner composes other native owners but its read-only HTTP cutover witness does not establish live generation, financial effects or remote Matrix execution

architecture atlas-provenance
  canonical_name AtlasProvenance
  family context
  domain Context
  maturity measured
  semantic_question When this atlas answers, what was it built from, and can that be checked from where it is being read?
  # The index is a build artifact that travels. A copy was installed on the
  # deployment once and then answered questions for four days about declarations
  # that had moved underneath it. Both copies look equally authoritative because
  # neither said when it was made -- and a planner told a capability is absent
  # rebuilds what already exists.
  node_types DeclarationDigest
  node_types IndexStamp
  edge_types built_from
  state_types verified
  state_types dated
  invariant the export stamps the index with a digest over every declaration byte it was built from, and atlas.mjs owns which bytes count so a second opinion cannot drift from it
  invariant where the declarations are present the index is checked and a disagreeing one is rebuilt rather than served; where they are absent it is dated instead, and every answer says which of the two happened
  invariant verifiability is decided by whether atlas.mjs is present, because that is the only place the index can be rebuilt; counting .yaff files instead made a deployment carrying two unrelated contract declarations claim it had verified an index against declarations that were never its inputs
  forbidden_inference a matching digest -> a correct atlas
  forbidden_inference a dated index -> a stale one, or a fresh one; dated means unverifiable from here
  computational_form derivation
  native_format json
  source_path architecture/atlas.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/tests/parity.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreAtlas/tests/parity.sh attests that the deployment answers at the digest just shipped and reports itself unverified rather than current
  measured the deployment answered from a 232-architecture index dated four days earlier while the checkout carried 258; get surface-ir returned architectural with one witness against implemented with five, and the deploy path now closes both
  measured a deliberately corrupted stamp caused the index to be regenerated and the true maturity served, rather than the corrupted one
  known_gap nothing runs the deploy on a schedule, so an index can still go stale between deploys; it can no longer do so silently

architecture claim-falsifiability
  canonical_name ClaimFalsifiability
  family context
  domain Context
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Where does this estate report a success it never checked?
  # Every defect repaired here over two days had one shape: a value naming a
  # condition, written so it can only say yes. cli_present asserted true on a
  # host with no aws binary; status "ok" printed beside endpoint_configured
  # false; a recipe counted four failures and returned zero; a database that
  # refused the connection was reported as having returned no rows. None is
  # subtle. They survive because nothing fails when they are wrong, which is the
  # definition of the class and the reason tripping over their consequences one
  # at a time is the slow way to find them.
  node_types Claim
  node_types Observation
  edge_types asserts
  edge_types observes
  state_types gated
  state_types advisory
  invariant a suite that counts its own failures exits on that count; this is the one pattern decidable without reading intent, because a test that cannot fail is never correct, and it is the only one the checker fails the build on
  invariant every other pattern is advisory and says so, because a literal true is right for a fact about the source and an unchecked exit is redundant beside a parse strict enough to fail closed; failing a build on those would be the unfalsifiable claim the checker exists to find
  invariant the checker scans code and never records; flagging generated projections and archived receipts buried thirty real findings under eleven hundred, which is this same failure committed by the tool
  forbidden_inference a flagged line -> a defect
  forbidden_inference a clean run -> an estate without unfalsifiable claims; it means these patterns do not appear
  computational_form derivation
  native_format text
  source_path architecture/check-falsifiable-claims.mjs
  witness a suite that counts failures and ends on its summary echo makes the checker exit 1; removing it returns the tree to exit 0
  measured of 21 candidates in the gated class, 20 were suites that correctly exit on their counter and one was not: live_e2e ran 33 checks against the live estate and returned 0 whatever it printed
  measured the advisory classes triaged to legitimate code -- resolve_binary_path really does test executability, the fulfillment closure really does have reachable false paths, and the pure tier's parse fails closed without consulting an exit status
  known_gap the checker reads patterns, not meaning; a claim expressed any other way passes it silently

architecture witness-grade
  canonical_name WitnessGrade
  family context
  domain Context
  maturity measured
  semantic_question For each architecture claiming to be measured, how strong is the backing, really?
  # The atlas enforces its first law existentially: a measured architecture must
  # name a witness and that witness must be openable. Existence is the weakest
  # standard there is. A witness that always passes satisfies it, a witness
  # nobody runs satisfies it, and a witness reading none of the state its
  # architecture is about satisfies it.
  node_types MaturityClaim
  node_types Witness
  edge_types backs
  state_types named
  state_types runnable
  state_types exercised
  state_types graded
  invariant the tiers are reported as a distribution and never as one number; a single figure would let 23 claims backed by a file nobody runs hide behind 6 that have been shown to fail
  invariant suite candidates are discovered from cmd/*/tests/*.sh and recursive tests/**/*.sh; directory membership does not establish execution or a passing result
  forbidden_inference a graded witness -> a correct architecture; mutation shows the witness reacts to the state it reads
  forbidden_inference an exercised witness -> an executed or load-bearing witness; the historical tier name means shell-suite discovery only
  computational_form derivation
  native_format text
  source_path architecture/check_witness_grade.py.archive
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/src/witness_grade.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAtlas/Makefile
  witness cmd/BonfyreAtlas/tests/witness-grade.sh compares recorded JS reports for mutation labels, missing and malformed receipts, symlinks, discovery depth and every tier; stale indexes cannot replace parsed YAFF
  known_gap mutation receipts are supplied evidence and are not authenticated; matching noticed_by labels does not establish when or where the suite ran
  known_gap the native port preserves recorded JSON receipt shapes; malformed non-array noticed_by fields are ignored as invalid receipts instead of treating strings as character sequences
  measured 2026-09-30 with no mutation receipt: 109 measured or proven claims, 0 graded, 48 exercised, 37 runnable but unrun, 24 named only
  measured of 61 architectures claiming measured or proven: 6 graded, 18 exercised, 23 runnable but unrun, 14 named in prose only
  measured 23 architectures claim measured on the strength of a witness file that nothing in this estate executes, and 14 on prose alone; the first law was being satisfied administratively for 37 of 61 claims
  known_gap only witnesses reachable from a local store can be graded; the suites that read the live estate over ssh are exercised and ungraded
  known_gap the distribution is graded 0, exercised 44, runnable 36, named 16. Nothing in ninety-six measured claims has been shown able to go red. `exercised` counts a witness that runs in the regression and has never failed, which is a statement about the regression and not about the witness; until a fact it reads is changed and it notices, a green suite and an empty suite are indistinguishable from outside.
  known_gap this grader existed and was not run. Two sessions of work added witnesses to a pile where nothing was graded, and the exposure was rediscovered by hand-written scans that got the numbers wrong twice before the real instrument was consulted. A tool nobody runs measures nothing.
